ng is -115  so these are just absolutely not a  audible concern  now typically when i run this test  especially on on dax that use akm chip  that doesn't have resampler the coax and  toslink inputs tend to do a lot worse  than usb  uh hopefully most of you are using usb  but sometimes you have a tv with  touchlink output and  or a game console what have you so  people care about that also  and here we see that performance  identical on all three so either has  extremely good clock generation  and extraction out of tossing and coax  or is resampling internally  and throwing out all the input jitter i  don't know which but either way  it's actually on result and it's just  very very nice to see uh  such good performance finally it is a  multi-tone test  a lot of people like this visually  kind of an attractive test in that we  take 32 tones  you can see their levels here and  run them through the dac digitally and  ask it to produce an analog output  and whatever shows up in between these  bands is intermodulation distortion  and an ideal dac would have infinite  troughs over here  and nothing in between them in practice  we get noise  from both the attack and my analyzer and  uh  we see that the uh the worst case noise  is 112  and distortion noise is minus 120  which is 20 bits already and then it  sinks  way down to almost 135 db  so that's exceptional performance for  any deck  let alone a bargain deck so net net  is another support product from topping  um  some people say i'm in their pocket for  some reason  i'll tell you there's no mystery in here  this is the uh  manual that came with with this stack  and  uh you know you you look at it hopefully  uh that's the case with this one yeah  look at the uh all the measurements in  there this looks surprisingly like mine  what does that mean the company has a  proper audio analyzer like my audio  precision there during the design and  they measure the performance and they  find problems and they fix them  other companies wait to for me to find  them the first time  because they haven't done their job  oftentimes the fixes are simple you may  have to just adjust the component  move something around isolate something  to get rid of noise  none of that costs money but you need to  have the tools to tell you that  you can't use your ears when the  distortions are so  low and noise levels are so low they're  way beyond threshold of hearing  so you want to you know do that in  design phase and when you do that then  you're going you have a great product  and my job's easy i'm just basically  confirming independently what they've  done  and performance is this good so there's  uh  you know no nothing else is needed over  here as far as trickery or what have you  just built a great product and you get  my praise for it  so that's it thanks for watching this is  my  first video on youtube thank you bye

